# [Bug]: Schema aware repair loses root $defs scope when validating an anyOf branch

### Version of the library

0.61.4

### Describe the bug

When malformed JSON activates the schema-aware repair parser, validation of an `anyOf` branch containing a root-relative $ref fails with `PointerToNowhere`:

```
jsonschema.exceptions._WrappedReferencingError: PointerToNowhere: '/$defs/Item' does not exist within {'type': 'array', 'items': {'$ref': '#/$defs/Item'}}
```

json_repair appears to validate the individual anyOf branch as a standalone schema document which fails because that isolated branch does not contain $defs.

### How to reproduce

```python
import json_repair

schema = {
    "$defs": {
        "Item": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
                "name": {"type": "string"},
            },
            "required": ["name"],
        }
    },
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
        "value": {
            "anyOf": [
                {
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {"$ref": "#/$defs/Item"},
                },
                {"type": "null"},
            ]
        }
    },
